nal initiation, translational termination, protein biosynthesis. RB genes are defined here by the following Gene Ontology terms: 35S primary transcript processing, ribosomal large subunit assembly and maintenance, rRNA metabolism, rRNA modification, rRNA processing, rRNA nucleus export, transcription from Pol I promoter, tRNA methylation, tRNA modification, tRNA processing, tRNA splicing, tRNA nucleus export, regulation of translation, processing of 20S pre-rRNA. <sup>&#x000a5;</sup>Up-regulated upon deletion of <italic>RPL12A </italic>(<italic>p </italic>&#x0003c; 10<sup>-24</sup>), <italic>RPL27A </italic>(<italic>p </italic>&#x0003c; 10<sup>-26</sup>), <italic>RPL34A </italic>(<italic>p </italic>&#x0003c; 10<sup>-8</sup>), <italic>RPL6B </italic>(<italic>p </italic>&#x0003c; 10<sup>-9</sup>), <italic>RPL8A </italic>(<italic>p </italic>&#x0003c; 10<sup>-63</sup>), or <italic>RPL24A </italic>(<italic>p </italic>&#x0003c; 10<sup>-20</sup>); see entries R135T, R137T, R138T, R139T, R140T, R141T in Additional data file 4.</p></table-wrap-foot></table-wrap></sec></back></article>